              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "==CP== = correct but may refuse. ==AP== = always answers but may be stale."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Strong vs Eventual Consistency",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Strong vs Eventual Consistency",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Strong vs eventual",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Strong (linearizable)",
                "Eventual"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "After a write returns",
                  "every later read sees it",
                  "reads can be {red:stale}"
                ],
                [
                  "Replicas",
                  "coordinate across nodes",
                  "converge if writes stop"
                ],
                [
                  "Cost",
                  "{red:higher latency}",
                  "{green:low latency}"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Middle models",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Read-your-writes==: you always see your own update",
                "==Monotonic reads==: never jump back to older data",
                "==Causal==: a reply never appears before its post",
                "A sane user view **without** full linearizability"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Convergence tools",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Last-write-wins==: clock-dependent, can **lose writes**",
                "==Vector clocks==: detect concurrent writes",
                "==CRDTs==: merge automatically, no lost updates",
                "==Read repair==: fix a stale replica during a read",
                "==Anti-entropy==: background replica comparison and sync"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "{green:Strong}",
                "{blue:Eventual}"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Balances",
                  "Feeds"
                ],
                [
                  "Inventory",
                  "Likes"
                ],
                [
                  "Uniqueness checks",
                  "Counters"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Money and uniqueness",
              "text": "Eventual consistency for ==balances, inventory or uniqueness checks== causes overspending and duplicates."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Quorums: R, W and N",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Quorums: R, W and N",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. The Three Numbers",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==N== = replica count",
                "==W== = acks needed for a write",
                "==R== = replicas consulted for a read",
                "Strong read rule: ==R + W > N==, so the read set overlaps the latest write set"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Tuning with N=3",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Setting",
                "Reads",
                "Writes",
                "Failures"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`W=2, R=2`",
                  "balanced",
                  "balanced",
                  "{green:tolerates 1}"
                ],
                [
                  "`W=3, R=1`",
                  "{green:fast}",
                  "{red:slowest}, strongest durability",
                  "writes fail if **any** replica is down"
                ],
                [
                  "`W=1, R=3`",
                  "slow",
                  "{green:fast}",
                  "reads need all 3"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Majority Quorum",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Majority = ==floor(N/2)+1==",
                "A cluster of ==2f+1== nodes survives **f** failures",
                "Use ==odd== sizes: an even node adds cost, not tolerance"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Nodes",
                "Majority",
                "Tolerates"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "3",
                  "2",
                  "1"
                ],
                [
                  "5",
                  "3",
                  "2"
                ],
                [
                  "6",
                  "4",
                  "{red:still 2}"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Common Mistake",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "R+W>N alone is not linearizable",
              "text": "It breaks with ==sloppy quorums==, ==hinted handoff== or clock-based ==last-write-wins== conflict resolution."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Rate Limiting Algorithms",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Rate Limiting Algorithms",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Purpose",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Cap ==requests per client== per time window",
                "Protects a service from **overload** and abuse",
                "Reject with ==HTTP 429== plus a `Retry-After` header"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. The Algorithms",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Refill",
                    "sub": "steady rate",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Bucket",
                    "sub": "up to capacity",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Request",
                    "sub": "spends 1 token",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Empty?",
                    "sub": "reject with 429",
                    "ink": "red"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Algorithm",
                "Bursts",
                "Trade-off"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "==Token bucket==",
                  "up to bucket size",
                  "most common choice"
                ],
                [
                  "Leaky bucket",
                  "none",
                  "queue drains at fixed rate, smooth output"
                ],
                [
                  "Fixed window",
                  "{red:2x at boundary}",
                  "simplest counter"
                ],
                [
                  "Sliding window log",
                  "exact",
                  "memory heavy"
                ],
                [
                  "Sliding window counter",
                  "approximate",
                  "cheap"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Shared Counters",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Keep counters in a ==shared store== like Redis",
                "Use atomic `INCR` or a **Lua script**",
                "Key by user, API key or IP"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "INCR rl:user42:12345",
                "EXPIRE rl:user42:12345 60"
              ],
              "note": "one key per client per window"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Per-instance counters",
              "text": "Each app instance counts alone, so the real limit grows with the instance count. Always use a ==shared store==."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Circuit Breakers and Retries with Backoff",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Circuit Breakers and Retries with Backoff",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Circuit Breaker States",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Closed",
                    "sub": "calls pass, failures counted",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Open",
                    "sub": "threshold hit: fail fast, no calls",
                    "ink": "red"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Half-Open",
                    "sub": "after timeout: few probes",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Probe succeeds → ==Closed==; probe fails → back to ==Open==",
                "Trip on ==failure-rate threshold== over a rolling window",
                "Tune: open duration, probe count",
                "Fail fast with a ==fallback== or cached response"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Retry with Backoff",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Wait ==base * 2^attempt==: 100ms, 200ms, 400ms ... cap 10s",
                "Always set a ==max attempt count==",
                "==Full jitter== = random(0, backoff): no synchronized retry waves"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "delay = min(cap, base * 2 ** attempt)",
                "time.sleep(random.uniform(0, delay))"
              ],
              "note": "full jitter"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Common Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Retrying non-idempotent calls without an ==idempotency key==",
                "Retrying ==4xx== errors",
                "Stacking retries at every layer"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Retry storm",
              "text": "3 layers x 3 tries = ==27 calls== on one failing request. Retry at one layer only."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
